        {
          "id": 2876909904,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Sorry for the slow response. \n\nThis seems correct to me.\n\nhttps://dev.mysql.com/doc/dev/mysql-server/latest/page_protocol_com_stmt_prepare.html has this:\n\n```\nif (packet_length >= 12) {\n  | int<2> | warning_count | Number of warnings |\n...\n}\n```\n\nMySQL 4.1 was released in 2004 and extended support for it ended in 2009 (~16 years ago). So I wonder if this was actual MySQL 4.1 or a different product that implements the same protocol or if this was more related to the `MYSQL_CAPS_CU` / `CLIENT_PROTOCOL_41` flag.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5884947,
            "username": "dveeden",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Daniël van Eeden",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/00c536bb5304097eb409787c4a770e820db2a200d04130b8ca03cbcda0f526f7?s=80&d=identicon",
